    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310-a1">

                <pb facs="0351" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg267"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Colon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                            1902</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of the Navy</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Everything is conceded. The United States guards and guarantees traffic and the
                    line of transit. To-day I permitted the exchange of Colombian troops from Panama
                    to Colon, about 1,000 men each way, the troops without arms in train guarded by
                    American naval force in the same manner as other passengers; arms and ammunition
                    in separate train, guarded also by naval force in the same manner as other
                    freight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McLean.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
